// D75 (revised, Plan 47) + [M-canceltoken-prelude-decl] (2026-07-13, Plan
// 173-хвост) followup — nested `supervised`/`spawn` scopes + CancelToken
// method calls (`.cancel()` / `.is_cancelled()`) in the SAME compile-unit as
// other prelude external types with same-shaped 0-effective-arg static
// constructors (`WriteBuffer.new()` — see d372_generic_static_default_cap.nv,
// already a folder-module peer of this file).
//
// Origin: Plan 198 REDO's large merged conformance corpus (nova-198 worktree,
// branch triage-198, ~1005+ peer files) flagged a suspected regression —
// user calls `tok.cancel()`/`tok.is_cancelled()` binding to a FOREIGN type
// (`WriteBuffer`/a local `Conn10`-shaped record) in some CU compositions,
// with an ICE variant (`is_cancelled` → emit_c.rs legacy `infer_call_ret_c`
// "[P67-LEGACY] method call return type unknown" panic) in the double-nested
// `supervised { spawn { supervised { spawn { ... } } } }` shape below.
//
// Investigation (Plan 173 fix-canceltoken-methods, 2026-07-13): triage-198's
// checkout LACKS today's `std/src/prelude/concurrency.nv` formal decl
// (confirmed via `git diff <main-base> triage-198-HEAD` — the file is wholly
// ABSENT on that branch, which only carries an EARLIER/partial attempt).
// Its corpus was exercised against the PRE-migration hardcoded-HashSet
// `CancelToken` (no `TypeDecl`, no method signatures) — the exact legacy
// arity-guessing class already diagnosed and fixed by `abc75b18f` /
// `96b3ac54c` / `454a78117` (see `d75_canceltoken_prelude_ctor.nv`'s header):
// a bigger merged CU just made the arity-collision more likely to land on
// `WriteBuffer`/a local record instead of `StringBuilder`. It is NOT a new
// checker defect surviving today's migration.
//
// Verification on this branch (main tip + 454a78117 applied): the exact two
// quarantined fixtures (nova-198 `fixtures/ice_blocked/
// nested_supervised_cancel.nv` — reproduced below — and `standalone/
// pos_fibers_per_worker_concurrent.nv`) both pass standalone AND merged into this
// folder-module's real single-CU gate (`nova test --positive
// --compile-error spec_tests/conformance`, entry `b11x_novaarray_user_ext_
// methods`) alongside `WriteBuffer`/`Conn10`-shaped types — no ICE, no
// mis-bind. This test locks that composition in permanently so a future
// regression is caught by the main gate instead of only a side corpus.
//
// Part of the SINGLE `spec_tests.conformance` folder-module.
module spec_tests.conformance

test "nested supervised with cancel token — cancel propagates (198-corpus composition)" {
    ro tok = CancelToken.new()
    mut inner_ran = AtomicBool.new(false)

    supervised(cancel: tok) {
        spawn {
            supervised {
                spawn {
                    inner_ran.store(true)
                    tok.cancel("inner cancel")
                }
            }
        }
    }

    // After supervised exits: tok was cancelled by inner spawn.
    assert(inner_ran.load())
    assert(tok.is_cancelled())
}

test "nested supervised with cancel token — normal completion (198-corpus composition)" {
    ro tok = CancelToken.new()
    mut result = AtomicInt.new(0)

    supervised(cancel: tok) {
        spawn {
            supervised {
                spawn { result.store(42) }
            }
        }
    }

    assert(result.load() == 42)
    assert(!tok.is_cancelled())
}
